{%- comment -%}
  The verdict word for a shelf color: the meaning, not the name of the ink, which tells a
  color-blind reader nothing -- and as bare text, because one call site is inside an `aria-label`
  where markup would turn a curator's typo into tag injection. The `else` is loud because
  `color: gren` used to fall through and publish "too early" for a shelf nobody had judged.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if color == 'green' -%}comprehensive
{%- elsif color == 'yellow' -%}partial
{%- elsif color == 'red' -%}too early
{%- else -%}[no verdict: {{ color | escape }}]
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign color = "" -%}
